Inputs (all exist, gate-passed; read schemas via a tiny read of ONE shard each, never scan dirs): J6 sites ~/orcd/scratch/feng/model_v2/j6_genome_v1 (11,002,701 rows; schema in ops/briefs/J6_FIX_RESULT.md, gate_report.json); J3 scores ~/orcd/scratch/feng/model_v2/j3_genome_v1 (256 shards, keyed by site id; channels complementarity/duplex/accessibility w/ status; 92 explicit failures; ops/briefs/J3_RESULT.md); J2 accessibility grids ~/orcd/scratch/feng/model_v2/j2_phase1,j2_phase2 (per-locus exon+-100, W/L/u variants; ops in jobs/j2_fold.py); J4 atlas ~/orcd/scratch/feng/model_v2/j4_atlas_v1/<config_id> (donor/acceptor sites, N-ablation raw deltas; sequence_ablation_proxy; config manifest ~/orcd/scratch/feng/model_v2/j4_configs/j4_configs_manifest.tsv); exon geometry from conference/model_v2/manifests/j2_loci_phase1.tsv + phase2. Conventions: trans_intervention.py, SCIENTIFIC_LOCK.md.
## J8: j8_feature_join.py
Deterministic, sharded, streaming (bounded memory) join of J6 sites x J3 channels, annotated with: distance (signed, strand-aware) from each J6 site to the nearest curated canonical exon donor/acceptor (from the J2/J4 exon manifests) and region class; J2 accessibility at the matching locus when the site falls inside a J2 locus (else explicit not_available, never fill); J4 N-ablation summary for the overlapping footprint when covered (else not_available). Every column carries evidence_class; failed/missing stay explicit (never 0); provenance/sha256 of every input shard in a manifest; atomic parquet + .done; idempotent; coordinate-assembly fence (GRCh38/v50). Row-count conservation test (output rows == J6 rows). No outcome data joins.
## J10: j10_robustness.py
(a) rank-stability engine: given a feature table and prespecified alternative settings (fold window variants, max_mismatch, duplex-energy channel vs complementarity, accessibility variants) compute for any candidate set the Kendall/Spearman rank agreement across alternatives, sign-flip frequency of pairwise orderings, and a stability flag; report instability explicitly. (b) null models: site/motif perturbation nulls (dinucleotide-preserving shuffles of the target flank, position-shifted decoy footprints in the same locus) giving empirical null distributions for each channel, with matched-GC/length decoys and a stated sampling universe; NO p-value is emitted unless the null's sampling universe is defined and n_decoys >= a stated minimum, else MetricBlocked-style refusal. (c) baseline-ablation harness (M0..M5 feature-family leave-out) that CALLS evaluation_core.py (already reviewed: use its guards; do not reimplement; it requires verified negatives for supervised metrics — here none exist, so produce descriptive rank-agreement only and say so). Deterministic seeds; tiny synthetic tests for every function; a sbatch for a bounded real run over the J9 SMN2 ASO set (F18/F14/F10; 3UP8 excluded) and over a few hundred real J6/J3 sites.
