     2	
     3	Coordinates are 1-based inclusive GRCh38/GENCODE v50. Geometry is relative to
     4	curated J2 exon interiors (the manifests include exactly 100 bases of padding).
     5	Distances use the footprint midpoint and transcript orientation. J4 overlap
     6	summaries are explicitly distinct from exact-footprint predictions. JSON feature
     7	cells retain alternative/context identity, status, evidence and missing values.
     8	
     9	The SQLite index checkpoints each verified input atomically. Its cache is 32 MiB;
    10	Arrow batches are bounded, but upstream Parquet footers also consume memory.
    11	Full indexing is a Slurm operation; --bounded selects an explicitly partial atlas.
    12	A measured full-genome index is ~37 GB, so --max-index-gib must be raised past its
    13	20 GiB default (see jobs/j8_full.sbatch for the per-source measurements).
    14	
    15	Known upstream coverage gap, not a defect here: J2 folded u in {8,12,18} while the
    16	ASO footprints are 10/14/18 nt, so only F18 sites (~0.01% of J6) can ever match a
    17	J2 grid cell exactly. Every other site's j2_accessibility is explicitly
    18	not_available; no length substitution is ever performed. J3's own per-footprint
    19	accessibility channel is unaffected and remains the usable accessibility source.
    20	"""
